From a4270ba9a9142d337cba08eaa0254ed6ea3b0fb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Belfry <belfry@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:18:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat(auth): key export for accounts without a password

Accounts created by preload-user and signed in through the OpenID Provider have no
password, so the export endpoint could never serve them. Every server-signed session now
carries an auth_time fact; POST /api/user/export-key lets a passwordless account export
within OIDC_REAUTH_WINDOW_SECS (default 300) of signing in, the same freshness the password
check provides for other accounts. GET /api/user/account reports has_password; the security
page offers "Sign in with Belfry to unlock" (a round trip through /api/auth/oidc/start) and
hides the password and e-mail sections for such accounts. verify-password answers 400 for
them instead of failing on the NULL password hash.
